cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its published evidence, please cite it as below."
title: "SpectraNS-3D: a reproducible numerical methodology for unforced 3D incompressible Navier–Stokes vortex-tube studies"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brahmbhatt
    given-names: Amit
    affiliation: Quantum-Clarity LLC
    email: amitb@quantum-clarity.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/amitb-quantum/spectrans-3d"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Validation-first Fourier pseudo-spectral solver and campaign evidence for
  unforced, positive-viscosity vortex tubes on the 2π-periodic cube. The release
  contains the audited solver, independent numerical tests, operational
  controllers, and a completed N512/N640/N768 study through t = 1.10 showing that
  integral quantities agree within 0.1% between N640 and N768 while stable local
  vorticity estimates remain resolution-sensitive at the 1–2% level. It is a
  finite-interval numerical study; it does not establish regularity, blowup or an
  enstrophy turnover. Documentation and figures are CC-BY-4.0.
keywords:
  - Navier–Stokes
  - pseudo-spectral
  - vortex tubes
  - enstrophy
  - numerical verification
  - reproducibility
  - GPU
